dayborder = 3,

visualreport=TRUE,

week_weekend_aggregate.part5 = TRUE,

frag.metrics = "all",

part5_agg2_60seconds = TRUE

)

Example 1

When running the
GGIR script for participant X, I got these results with rather low PA (LPA en
MPA) levels and high sedentary behavior levels. However this participant is a
nurse where it is expected that she performs more LPA. I asked this participant
for more feedback on her week and she stated that she had a rather active week
with a lot of walking activity during her working hours.

Therefore, I think that these results give rather an OVERestimation of SB. Next, I uploaded the data in Actilife to explore her results. The blue lines indicate activity intensities where this graph shows rather active days. (period marked in red is the sleeping period)

Example 2

Participant Y has a rather active
behavior profile with rather small sedentary behavior levels (only 96 minutes a
day) when interpreting the output in GGIR. However, this person has a sedentary job where he sits a lot during the
working hours. This person questions his GGIR results as sedentary behavior could represents
an UNDERestimation.

As I explore his file in Actilife, I got the following result.
The blue lines indicate that he has some active periods but also longer periods
of sedentary behavior. This is inconsistent with the  results out of GGIR.

Thanks in advance for your time.

Kind regards,

Iris Willems

